  "body": "What happens: since v0.25.0 (2026-11-22), user-facing features and settings merged without a change to the user guide (`site/content/guide/`). The next cut (v0.26.0) regenerates the documentation site from the tagged tree, so these ship undocumented. Same shape as #2854 (v0.25.0).\n\nFeatures without guide text (PR, where it belongs):\n- #3151 V-Carve operation: depth from the region width along the medial axis - operations/operations-2d.md (new section)\n- #2822 Rest machining on 2D Pocket from the previous operations - operations/operations-2d.md\n- #3220 Deburr: chord width, Constant Depth sizing and multi-pass breaks (**breaking**) - wherever Deburr is described\n- #3057 Place DXF profiles on the stock from the Stock page (and by drop) - set-up/setups.md, operations-2d.md\n- #3158 Cutting data for wood, MDF, plywood, acrylic and HDPE - set-up/tools.md (materials)\n- #3279 Router machine kind shows the router options on the Milling tab - check-and-post/machines.md\n- #3280 Fanuc AI contour control option (G05.1 Q1 R / Q0) - check-and-post/posting.md (Fanuc options)\n- #3307 Fanuc option to write the stock as a Manual Guide i blank (G1902 / G1900) - check-and-post/posting.md\n\nUser-visible settings and messages from fix PRs:\n- #3386 Boundary: separate \"Inside boundary offset\" and \"Outside boundary offset\" - operations/boundaries (or wherever Boundary is described)\n- #3232 Wire Contour: sharp inside corners allowed at the wire radius (option, default off) - operations/operations-wire.md\n- #3108 A 3D Adaptive that falls back to Offset rings now raises a warning - operations/operations-3d.md, check-and-post (warnings)\n- #3113 Circular climbs to clearance between its rings - operations/operations-2d.md (Circular)\n\nEach feature gets: what it does, where the control is, one example or screenshot where the guide uses them, and any refusal message a user can hit. Re-run this list at the start of the cut (`git log v0.25.0..main`, feat PRs with no `site/content/guide` change) and add what merged since.\n\n**Done means:** every PR above has guide text in `site/content/guide/`, the site builds (`zola build` in `site/`), and the site tests pass.\n",
